## [ENT-178] | 2026-11-17 18:29 UTC | Unity | general | ref: governance/rulebook.md | see: ENT-177
Rule F9 refined minutes later on Suggi's word ("not just hull and shield but also weapons firepower ... both are important; ship level also"). The rulebook's F9 is the text in force; ENT-177's single gauge is replaced.
- Two gauges, a creature must pass both. Firepower = the side's weapon damage per tick, +1% per level of each pilot's Gunnery, Weapons and Tactics (the catalog's bonus_per_level); the side kills a creature of at most 7 times its firepower in hull. Toughness = the side's hull plus shield as the game reports them; the creature weighs at most half of it (a predator twice its hull). Ship level counts through both (tier: hull, shield, slots; skills: both gauges).
